pan="1">ADC GLRLM SRE</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.10 (0.02, 0.30)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;.001</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tblfn5"><p>Accuracy from 10-fold cross-validation with five repeats.</p></fn><fn id="tblfn6"><p>Abbreviations: AIC = Akaike information criterion; CI = confidence interval; OR = odds ratio.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><p>Models trained in the prediction of lymph node involvement based on N stage (N1), the highest training accuracy and best model fit were from the imaging-based T2w&#x02009;+&#x02009;PET hybrid model (mean accuracy&#x02009;=&#x02009;0.773, AIC&#x02009;=&#x02009;99.0), demonstrating associations with T2w CONVENTIONAL Kurtosis (OR&#x02009;=&#x02009;4.01, 95% CI&#x02009;=&#x02009;1.06, 19.4, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x02009;=&#x02009;.06) and PET70% DISCRETIZED TLG (OR&#x02009;=&#x02009;4.89, 95% CI&#x02009;=&#x02009;1.02, 30.9, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x02009;=&#x02009;.07) variables (<xref rid="tqaf014-T4" ref-type="table">Table&#x000a0;4</xref>).</p><table-wrap position="float" id="tqaf014-T4"><label>Table 4.</label><caption><p>N Stage (N1) final logistic regression model estimates and accuracy from training data.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><colgroup span="1"><col valign="top" align="left" span="1"/><col valign="top" align="left" span="1"/><col valign="top" align="left" span="1"/><col valign="top" align="left" span="1"/><col valign="top" align="left" span="1"/><col valign="top" align="left" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Variables</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">OR (95% CI)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">
